1366
00:59:26.070 --> 00:59:27.440
In one form or another,

1367
00:59:27.440 --> 00:59:30.250
I think we all have to have a hero's journey

1368
00:59:30.250 --> 00:59:33.303
or many hero's journeys, one after another.

1369
00:59:34.500 --> 00:59:38.840
And I think a lot of maybe what is going wrong today

1370
00:59:38.840 --> 00:59:41.654
in this country is people aren't living out

1371
00:59:41.654 --> 00:59:44.330
their hero's journey 'cause they,

1372
00:59:44.330 --> 00:59:46.080
somehow they don't have to,

1373
00:59:46.080 --> 00:59:50.845
it's not, life, it's easy enough now.

1374
00:59:50.845 --> 00:59:53.310
People can get by that they don't have to do that.

1375
00:59:53.310 --> 00:59:55.780
And also, obviously the force of resistance

1376
00:59:55.780 --> 00:59:57.600
is trying to stop them from doing that.

1377
00:59:57.600 --> 00:59:59.903
But I would, there's,

1378
01:00:00.767 --> 01:00:05.270
Walker Percy is a great kind of writing hero of mine

1379
01:00:05.270 --> 01:00:09.630
and he wrote a book, I'm blanking on the name of it now,

1380
01:00:09.630 --> 01:00:11.987
but in the book, it's not "The Moviegoer,"

1381
01:00:13.028 --> 01:00:15.060
the character is a doctor and he has

1382
01:00:16.415 --> 01:00:19.937
a couple that come to him and they're a married couple

1383
01:00:19.937 --> 01:00:22.270
