various other warrior cultures.

1536
01:07:07.580 --> 01:07:09.000
And it was a surprise to me.

1537
01:07:09.000 --> 01:07:09.833
It's like I say to myself,

1538
01:07:09.833 --> 01:07:11.520
"Well, why am I writing about this?"

1539
01:07:11.520 --> 01:07:14.433
It's not like, I'm not a Navy SEAL.

1540
01:07:14.433 --> 01:07:16.950
Why did I write about this?

1541
01:07:16.950 --> 01:07:21.500
And I think that it's the inner war, the writer's war,

1542
01:07:21.500 --> 01:07:23.650
the artist's war that we were talkin' about

1543
01:07:24.730 --> 01:07:29.730
that in a way you, to face the blank page,

1544
01:07:32.480 --> 01:07:34.820
to write a book, to write a movie, to write whatever it is,

1545
01:07:34.820 --> 01:07:37.050
or ultra endurance, things like that,

1546
01:07:37.050 --> 01:07:39.250
you have to be a warrior.

1547
01:07:39.250 --> 01:07:42.950
One way or another you've gotta take the warrior virtues

1548
01:07:42.950 --> 01:07:47.950
which I would name as courage, patience, comradery,

1549
01:07:48.530 --> 01:07:51.910
love for one's brothers and sisters, selflessness,

1550
01:07:51.910 --> 01:07:55.770
and very important, the willing embracing of adversity

1551
01:07:55.770 --> 01:07:57.020
and there are a lot of other virtues

1552
01:07:57.020 --> 01:08:00.490
but those virtues that a warrior, a Spartan warrior

1553
01:08:00.490 --> 01:08:03.841
or Alexander the Great would use it for enemies out there,

1554
01:08:03.841 --> 01:08:06.692
the artist or the endurance athlete uses

1555
01:08:06.692 --> 01:08:10.890
those virtues to get against the enemies in here, right?

1556
01:08:10.890 --> 01:08:14.910
When you're on your fourth Ironman in a row,

1557
01:08:14.910 --> 01:08:18.317
and every fiber of your being is screaming out,

1558
01:08:18.317 --> 01:08:21.580
"Stop, stop, this is insane,"

1559
01:08:21.580 --> 01:08:23.990
you're having to call upon something, right?

1560
01:08:23.990 --> 01:08:28.610
And I think it's that sort of, that warrior mentality,

1561
01:08:28.610 --> 01:08:31.182
the same thing that the Spartans called

1562
01:08:31.182 --> 01:08:35.000
on when the day three at Thermopylae, whatever.

1563
01:08:35.000 --> 01:08:39.710
So, I guess, again, I was sort of drawn to write these books

1564
01:08:39.710 --> 01:08:41.490
and I didn't even know why

1565
01:08:41.490 --> 01:08:43.340
but I think I was kind of reinforcing

1566
01:08:43.340 --> 01:08:47.000
for myself in a way that kind of code,

1567
01:08:47.000 --> 01:08:50.270
that code of honor, that sense of shame,

1568
01:08:50.270 --> 01:08:52.824
and that ability to kind of endure

1569
01:08:52.824 --> 01:08:57.824
and to keep going forward into into the unknown.

1570
01:08:58.460 --> 01:08:59.293
Yeah.

1571
01:08:59.293 --> 01:09:01.841
The idea of being regimented of having

1572
01:09:01.841 --> 01:09:06.841
a core code of ethics to which

1573
01:09:08.020 --> 01:09:11.630
you organize your life is what's required

1574
01:09:11.630 --> 01:09:14.670
to express yourself as an artist

1575
01:09:14.670 --> 01:09:18.360
which I think is anathema for somebody who's unfamiliar

1576
01:09:18.360 --> 01:09:20.090
because they think, "Oh, artists are just,

1577
01:09:20.090 --> 01:09:22.547
they're free thinking and they just create,

1578
01:09:22.547 --> 01:09:25.580
and it's all very flowery,"
Yeah, right, yeah.

1579
01:09:25.580 --> 01:09:30.010
whereas you've imposed almost a military discipline

1580
01:09:30.010 --> 01:09:34.870
and structure upon this process to demystify it

1581
01:09:34.870 --> 01:09:37.970
so that you can allow for the mystical to enter

1582
01:09:39.710 --> 01:09:43.980
and how that plays into what it means to be a warrior.

1583
01:09:43.980 --> 01:09:46.040
It's like the warriors,

1584
01:09:46.040 --> 01:09:48.300
the warrior's obstacles are external.

1585
01:09:48.300 --> 01:09:50.853
The artists' obstacles are internal,

1586
01:09:52.000 --> 01:09:56.330
but the warrior on the battlefield

1587
01:09:56.330 --> 01:10:00.380
has to have mastery over that sense of self,

1588
01:10:00.380 --> 01:10:03.110
that like interconnectedness in order

1589
01:10:03.110 --> 01:10:06.498
to combat those external forces of resistance.

1590
01:10:06.498 --> 01:10:08.266
Is that how you did that?
Yes, the other thing

1591
01:10:08.266 --> 01:10:11.180
is that I think in a military context,

1592
01:10:11.180 --> 01:10:14.350
usually that discipline or that mastery

1593
01:10:14.350 --> 01:10:16.460
is imposed from without, right?

1594
01:10:16.460 --> 01:10:18.170
You've got sergeants or lieutenants

1595
01:10:18.170 --> 01:10:20.070
or whatever that are teaching you or that,

1596
01:10:20.070 --> 01:10:24.190
and you're in a structure that is shaming you

1597
01:10:24.190 --> 01:10:27.300
and making you go forward, right?

1598
01:10:27.300 --> 01:10:29.410
From outside externally.

1599
01:10:29.410 --> 01:10:32.338
Whereas, and I think this is one of the reasons why

1600
01:10:32.338 --> 01:10:34.660
a lotta guys and gals who leave

1601
01:10:34.660 --> 01:10:35.927
the military have a hard time

1602
01:10:35.927 --> 01:10:37.870
is when you make the switch

1603
01:10:37.870 --> 01:10:42.220
to being an artist or an entrepreneur or a fitness athlete,

1604
01:10:42.220 --> 01:10:44.770
that now become self-discipline.

1605
01:10:44.770 --> 01:10:45.603
Right.

1606
01:10:45.603 --> 01:10:46.436
Nobody's giving you

1607
01:10:46.436 --> 01:10:47.360
the orders.
Self reinforcement,

1608
01:10:47.360 --> 01:10:48.600
self validation.

1609
01:10:48.600 --> 01:10:52.456
And that's a big, hard change to make.

1610
01:10:52.456 --> 01:10:55.900
That's a whole other dimension of reality.

1611
01:10:55.900 --> 01:10:56.733
Right.

1612
01:10:56.733 --> 01:11:00.885
You're not accountable to the lieutenant

1613
01:11:00.885 --> 01:11:04.740
or the general or whoever, but only to yourself.

1614
01:11:04.740 --> 01:11:06.230
The other thing, and I'm sure this is true

1615
01:11:06.230 --> 01:11:07.130
in endurance sports too,

1616
01:11:07.130 --> 01:11:10.040
is there's an element of drudgery in this, right?

1617
01:11:10.040 --> 01:11:13.668
And being able to embrace the drudgery,

1618
01:11:13.668 --> 01:11:16.500
to train, you gotta go out on the trail, da da da.

1619
01:11:16.500 --> 01:11:18.897
Yet another day I gotta get up, right?

1620
01:11:18.897 --> 01:11:21.210
Right.
Same thing in writing

1621
01:11:21.210 --> 01:11:22.930
or any creative enterprise.

1622
01:11:22.930 --> 01:11:25.096
There are times when it's just a slog,

1623
01:11:25.096 --> 01:11:27.957
but again, that's a kind of a warrior virtue too.

1624
01:11:27.957 --> 01:11:30.290
The warrior learns to, and the soldier learns

1625
01:11:30.290 --> 01:11:32.143
to just keep shovelin', keep diggin' the ditch.

1626
01:11:32.143 --> 01:11:34.630
It's no fun, there's no glamor,

1627
01:11:34.630 --> 01:11:36.443
but that's what it is.
Not the chain gang.

1628
01:11:36.443 --> 01:11:37.370
Yeah.

1629
01:11:37.370 --> 01:11:42.010
Yeah, but that's how anything is created, right?

1630
01:11:42.010 --> 01:11:42.843
Is it not?
Yes.

1631
01:11:42.843 --> 01:11:44.910
I mean, you have to show up day in and day out

1632
01:11:44.910 --> 01:11:46.760
and most days aren't so great.

1633
01:11:46.760 --> 01:11:48.458
And every once in a while you get that spark

1634
01:11:48.458 --> 01:11:50.960
and it's awesome and you live for that,

1635
01:11:50.960 --> 01:11:55.900
