1638
01:12:00.769 --> 01:12:03.180
or crossing any finish line.

1639
01:12:03.180 --> 01:12:05.750
It is truly just about the showing up.

1640
01:12:05.750 --> 01:12:07.390
Now, did you always feel that way, Rich,

1641
01:12:07.390 --> 01:12:08.880
or was that somethin' that you learned,

1642
01:12:08.880 --> 01:12:11.640
when you were doin' all of those Ironman's and stuff,

1643
01:12:11.640 --> 01:12:13.840
did you have that attitude

1644
01:12:13.840 --> 01:12:15.300
or was that something that evolved

1645
01:12:15.300 --> 01:12:16.959
through the course?
No, I mean,

1646
01:12:16.959 --> 01:12:20.517
I didn't get into it to like beat people or win races.

1647
01:12:20.517 --> 01:12:22.860
I really, I did have enough self-awareness

1648
01:12:22.860 --> 01:12:24.550
around it to know that I was getting into it

1649
01:12:24.550 --> 01:12:26.650
as a process of self discovery.

1650
01:12:26.650 --> 01:12:29.560
Ah, good for you.
I'm competitive with myself,

1651
01:12:29.560 --> 01:12:31.567
not with anyone else, but I learned,

1652
01:12:31.567 --> 01:12:35.910
I love the suffering and the mental

1653
01:12:35.910 --> 01:12:38.550
and physical challenge of the whole thing.

1654
01:12:38.550 --> 01:12:40.430
And I learned that as a young person, as a swimmer.

1655
01:12:40.430 --> 01:12:44.960
So, I had that kind of language for myself

1656
01:12:44.960 --> 01:12:49.960
before I got into ultra endurance and understood deeply

1657
01:12:50.530 --> 01:12:53.010
that it's about process and the slog,

1658
01:12:53.010 --> 01:12:55.360
like that's how I got to where I got as a swimmer.

1659
01:12:55.360 --> 01:12:57.880
That's how I, achieved academic,

1660
01:12:57.880 --> 01:13:00.990
like anything good that I've ever done has been about that.

1661
01:13:00.990 --> 01:13:04.562
So, that wasn't a lesson that needed to be taught to me.

1662
01:13:04.562 --> 01:13:05.890
I've always gotten that

1663
01:13:05.890 --> 01:13:07.262
and that's how I've approached the podcast

1664
01:13:07.262 --> 01:13:08.780
and everything else that I've done.

1665
01:13:08.780 --> 01:13:10.360
Like, I'm good at grinding.

1666
01:13:10.360 --> 01:13:12.860
Like if I have a talent, it's not athletic,

1667
01:13:12.860 --> 01:13:14.610
it's just I'm willing to suffer

1668
01:13:14.610 --> 01:13:16.830
and work harder than the next guy

1669
01:13:16.830 --> 01:13:19.390
and put in the grind when no one's looking.

1670
01:13:19.390 --> 01:13:21.140
And I think that's the secret sauce

1671
01:13:21.140 --> 01:13:22.364
and I've said this many times before,

1672
01:13:22.364 --> 01:13:25.768
but most people really wildly overestimate

1673
01:13:25.768 --> 01:13:28.430
what they can do in a year or so,

1674
01:13:28.430 --> 01:13:31.120
and overestimate what they can do in a year

1675
01:13:31.120 --> 01:13:33.210
and wildly underestimate what they can do in a decade

1676
01:13:33.210 --> 01:13:35.350
and as somebody who didn't publish their first book

1677
01:13:35.350 --> 01:13:38.400
until they were in their 50s and now has 20 books,

1678
01:13:38.400 --> 01:13:41.840
you're a living Testament to that sentiment.

1679
01:13:41.840 --> 01:13:42.673
Yeah, I'm what you

1680
01:13:42.673 --> 01:13:43.903
would term a grinder.
Yeah.

1681
01:13:43.903 --> 01:13:47.420
Like if that's a talent, if I have any talent, it's that.

1682
01:13:47.420 --> 01:13:50.161
But I am willing to get at the grindstone

1683
01:13:50.161 --> 01:13:51.770
and just keep hammering.

1684
01:13:51.770 --> 01:13:53.795
When I think of a younger version of you,

1685
01:13:53.795 --> 01:13:57.190
I think of Ryan Holiday, who actually introduced us,

1686
01:13:57.190 --> 01:13:58.550
thank you, Ryan,
Ah, yes.

1687
01:13:58.550 --> 01:13:59.680
for making the introduction,

1688
01:13:59.680 --> 01:14:02.240
but that's a guy who shows up for the page every day,

1689
01:14:02.240 --> 01:14:03.090
is very clear
Oh, he does, yeah.

1690
01:14:03.090 --> 01:14:04.300
that this is what he's here to do.

1691
01:14:04.300 --> 01:14:06.441
He's here to write books and he doesn't get caught

1692
01:14:06.441 --> 01:14:10.190
up in all the stuff that swirls around it.

1693
01:14:10.190 --> 01:14:12.380
Like, as soon as a book's done he's onto the next book

1694
01:14:12.380 --> 01:14:15.340
and the guy's crankin' out a book a year

1695
01:14:15.340 --> 01:14:17.560
and I see the same discipline

1696
01:14:17.560 --> 01:14:21.750
and approach to craft that you have.

1697
01:14:21.750 --> 01:14:23.233
Yeah, I'm amazed that Ryan does that

1698
01:14:23.233 --> 01:14:24.335
at such a young age.

1699
01:14:24.335 --> 01:14:27.553
It's unbelievable.
Really, how did he do that?

1700
01:14:27.553 --> 01:14:28.545
I don't know.

1701
01:14:28.545 --> 01:14:31.260
I don't know, the level of the, yeah.

1702
01:14:31.260 --> 01:14:33.221
And it's discipline.

1703
01:14:33.221 --> 01:14:34.967
He has a structure and a system

1704
01:14:34.967 --> 01:14:36.770
