Yeah, maybe he was struck

1754
01:16:30.610 --> 01:16:32.410
by lightening when he first got the flash

1755
01:16:32.410 --> 01:16:34.490
of what that melody was,

1756
01:16:34.490 --> 01:16:36.789
but then it took forever to get

1757
01:16:36.789 --> 01:16:38.697
it down exactly the way he wanted it.

1758
01:16:38.697 --> 01:16:40.660
Right, so let's talk a little bit

1759
01:16:40.660 --> 01:16:43.786
more about that transition between amateur

1760
01:16:43.786 --> 01:16:46.668
or dilettante and "Turning Pro," right?

1761
01:16:46.668 --> 01:16:50.940
Which is the great follow-up to "The War of Art",

1762
01:16:50.940 --> 01:16:54.590
like this difference in, it's really a mindset shift, right?

1763
01:16:54.590 --> 01:16:56.720
Like, am I doing this as a side thing?

1764
01:16:56.720 --> 01:16:57.900
Or is this who I am?

1765
01:16:57.900 --> 01:17:00.069
And if so, what is my relationship

1766
01:17:00.069 --> 01:17:03.060
to the work I wanna create?

1767
01:17:03.060 --> 01:17:07.810
I mean, for me having defined resistance

1768
01:17:07.810 --> 01:17:10.170
as this negative force, then the next question becomes,

1769
01:17:10.170 --> 01:17:11.263
well, how do you get around it?

1770
01:17:11.263 --> 01:17:13.330
How do you overcome it?

1771
01:17:13.330 --> 01:17:16.530
And for me, it was the idea

1772
01:17:16.530 --> 01:17:20.390
of turning pro by which I mean that,

1773
01:17:20.390 --> 01:17:24.130
not that you only will work for money from now on

